Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraSceneMultiway", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"4d6322e5-d909-4758-829b-25b207783284"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraSceneMultiway"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSceneMultiway", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["scene", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["graph", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a8bb95e8-8208-4114-82f9-6b81c8781b64"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "explores exact finite construction states and retains their incoming \
events.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"ab15bfa0-4137-4ce3-915a-ebc76f02f815"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraSceneMultiway"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSceneMultiway", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["scene", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["graph", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["bindings", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["options", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f9c2963d-755a-4745-8a8c-27334987775f"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "starts with fixed bindings."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"87df12b2-de6b-44a1-b759-075c361501ed"],

Cell["\<\
This is an eager finite explorer for small simple undirected unweighted \
graphs. Each pool comes from its construction's named token sampler with All. \
The scene must carry valid ScheduleValidity provenance. Rebuild an older \
descriptor from its original object and hypothesis syntax. Unsupported \
schedules, selectors and domains stay unevaluated.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b38677a1-2675-4579-99b7-9b725a1cc41c"],

Cell["\<\
States merge only when completed-construction IDs and exact labeled bindings \
agree. Declared sets normalize, while point labels, walk order, repeated \
traversals and Graph carriers retain their kinds. All incoming accepted or \
fixed events survive merging. Pending assertions remain undecided; \
unsupported assertions cannot certify an empty solution set.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"056649c8-0f67-459c-a84b-deb04b04f66b"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an Association containing States, Events, StateGraph, Layers, \
StepLayers, Instances, Expansions, Frontier, Completeness, Diagnostics and \
saved scene/substrate/settings. Event layers count individual constructions. \
StepLayers are completed group boundaries. Final or requested-prefix \
instances are distinct from an unfinished event-depth frontier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"08489a47-1059-4cad-9269-7a72929ecb0c"],

Cell["\<\
Options \"Steps\" (All), \"MaxDepth\", \"MaxStates\", \"MaxEvents\", \
\"MaxCandidates\" and \"MaxTime\" (Infinity) bound the request. Candidate \
limits bound examinations, not eager All-pool acquisition or temporary \
memory. State, event and candidate frontiers retain their exact unfinished \
obligations. Requested-prefix and whole-scene completeness are separate; \
known state vertices alone do not certify missing incoming events. There is \
no resumability or hard memory ceiling. User-supplied geometry profiles must \
be pure and deterministic. This assumption is not enforced: an effectful \
callback can consume random state during pool acquisition.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0cf9760b-3659-4ac1-b51b-2e73dddf7d09"]
}, Open  ]],

